## Done-Coding SOP

```
1. /simplify (or your equivalent)   # clean up changed code
2. /review (or your equivalent)     # peer code review
3. <your test command> -q           # must be green
4. commit on feature branch
5. git checkout main && git merge --ff-only <branch>
6. git branch -d <branch> && git worktree prune
7. git push origin main
```

Full rules: [renaissance-rigor-playbook/ship-or-sink-rules.md](renaissance-rigor-playbook/ship-or-sink-rules.md).

**If any orchestrated/automated execution workflow exists, verify it actually calls step 1-2 — don't assume.** (The source project learned this the hard way: three phases landed on `main` with the simplify step silently skipped because the automated workflow never called it; the manual SOP text alone wasn't load-bearing.)

