## How to Use This Template

1. Fill in every `<bracketed>` placeholder with real project content. Delete a section entirely if your project has no equivalent (e.g. no APR if you have no tunable numeric parameters yet) rather than leaving a placeholder-only section live.
2. Copy `docs/renaissance-rigor-playbook/` into your new project's `docs/` directory unchanged, alongside this file (renamed to `CLAUDE.md`, in your repo root).
3. As real content accumulates (a real glossary, a real gotchas file, real DAG invariants), grow this file the way the source project's CLAUDE.md grew — a line here that indexes into a full doc, never the full doc's content inlined into this file. Keep CLAUDE.md as a dense index; let `docs/foundation/` carry the depth.
4. Version this file (`**Version:**` header) and bump it on structural changes, mirroring the source project's own convention.
